===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|en|enm|as}}, from {{der|en|fro|as}}, from {{der|en|la|as}}, {{m|la|assis||unity, copper coin, the unit of coinage}}. {{doublet|en|as}}. Likely related or deriving ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁éǵʰs}}, or otherwise taking from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-||sharp, pointed}} in the sense of "singular". Or it could be derived from Etruscan.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|card games}} A [[playing card]] showing a single [[pip]], typically the highest or lowest ranking card in a game.
#* {{quote-song|en|artist=w:Tex Ritter|date=1948-01-01|album=Famous Country Music Makers|track=20|title=Deck of Cards|url=https://genius.com/Tex-ritter-deck-of-cards-lyrics|passage=You see, Sir, when I look at the '''Ace''' it reminds me that there is but one God. The deuce reminds me that the bible is divided into two parts; the Old and New Testaments. And when I see the trey I think of the Father, Son and Holy Ghost.}}
# {{lb|en|dice}} A [[die]] [[face]] marked with a single dot, typically representing the number one.
# The ball marked with the number 1 in [[pool]] and related games.
#* '''1961''', ''The Hustler'' (film): a character is calling his next shot
#*: '''Ace''' in the corner.
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} A [[dollar bill]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1990|author=David F. Friedman; Don DeNevi|title=A Youth in Babylon: Confessions of a Trash-film King|page=136
|passage={{...}} maybe two or three twenties, a dozen tens, and twenty or thirty fins. The rest is all '''aces''' and silver.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1996|author=Arthur M. Smith; Robert Thomas King|title=Let's Get Going|page=65
|passage=If they got too many '''aces''' (dollar bills) or fives or tens, they turned them in to the vault where they became part of the reserve.}}
# A very small quantity or degree; a [[particle]]; an [[atom]]; a [[jot]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:modicum}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=c. 1658|author=Dr. Henry More|title=Government of the Tongue
|passage=He will not bate an '''ace''' of absolute certainty.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Spanish Fryar|45|I'LL not wag an '''ace''' farther: The whole World ſhall not bribe me to it;}}
# {{lb|en|tennis|volleyball}} A [[serve]] won without the opponent hitting the ball.
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[point]] won by a single [[stroke]], as in [[handball]], [[rackets]], etc.
# {{lb|en|US|baseball}} The best [[pitcher]] on the [[team]].
# {{lb|en|US|baseball|dated|19th century}} A [[run]].
# {{lb|en|US|golf|disc golf}} A [[hole in one]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Arv Olson|title=Backspin: 120 Years of Golf in British Columbia|page=253
|passage="Most of the '''aces''' weren't on holes I would have liked to have made them on," confessed Colk, who dropped his fifth dodo of 1935 on December 29, which was believed at the time to be a record for most '''aces''' in a year.}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes|_|attributive}} An [[expert]] at something; a [[maverick]], [[genius]]; a person of supreme talent.
#: {{syn|en|expert|wiz|Thesaurus:skilled person}}
#: {{co|en|an '''ace''' detective}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1932|year_published=1965|author=w:Delos W. Lovelace|title=[[w:King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong]]|page=4|passage=‘Weston, the '''ace''' of theatrical agents.’}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 29, 2011
|author=Jon Smith
|title=Tottenham 3 - 1 Shamrock Rovers
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15014632.stm
|page=
|passage=Mexican '''ace''' Dos Santos smashed home the third five minutes later after good work from Defoe.}}
# A military aircraft [[pilot]] who is credited with shooting down many enemy aircraft, typically five or more.
# {{lb|en|US}} A perfect [[score]] on a school exam.
# Any of various [[hesperiid]] butterflies.
# {{lb|en|physics|obsolete}} A [[quark]].

